WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.170
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.270 --> 00:02.200
[The characters, behaviors, locations, organizations, professions,

3
00:02.220 --> 00:04.150
and events depicted in this series are entirely fictional

4
00:04.170 --> 00:06.160
and created for entertainment purposes only.

5
00:06.180 --> 00:08.110
No harm or illegal action is intended to be promoted or encouraged.

6
00:08.130 --> 00:10.000
Viewer discretion is advised.]

7
00:10.560 --> 00:13.050
The last time I had anything to do with chemistry

8
00:13.070 --> 00:14.370
was in grade 12.

9
00:14.390 --> 00:16.290
But the chemistry I studied back then,

10
00:16.310 --> 00:18.560
and the chemistry between us right now

11
00:18.580 --> 00:20.180
are completely different.

12
00:20.200 --> 00:21.410
Absolutely, Giew.

13
00:21.440 --> 00:25.120
Uh... So we're bringing back the long take shot.

14
00:25.570 --> 00:27.570
Let me check if that's possible...

15
00:27.590 --> 00:28.590
That's not possible, Jane!

16
00:28.640 --> 00:29.470
Ow.

17
00:30.860 --> 00:33.570
Uh... At any rate, I need to talk to my team first

18
00:33.600 --> 00:36.580
to see how much we can get done, because we don't have much time,

19
00:36.600 --> 00:38.790
and the schedule is very tight.

20
00:38.810 --> 00:41.200
We'll update you as soon as possible.

21
00:44.380 --> 00:45.220
Hey, Jane.

22
00:45.410 --> 00:47.460
I included the long take in the first draft,

23
00:47.480 --> 00:48.290
- but they... - Jaab.

24
00:52.680 --> 00:54.950
They didn't want it.

25
00:55.290 --> 00:56.770
So I removed it from the board.

26
00:56.790 --> 00:59.140
We made a few adjustments... until the final draft.

27
00:59.160 --> 01:01.150
We're shooting in the next two days,

28
01:01.170 --> 01:03.090
and they haven't told us to add anything else.

29
01:03.110 --> 01:05.310
We were just updating them on the costume references,

30
01:05.330 --> 01:06.600
and now, suddenly, they want a long take.

31
01:06.620 --> 01:07.370
Come on!

32
01:07.390 --> 01:09.780
This is an advertisement project, not a made-to-order dish.

33
01:10.010 --> 01:11.460
It's just too much, isn't it?

34
01:12.080 --> 01:13.570
Jaab, you've lost it again.

35
01:13.800 --> 01:15.610
I was on the phone with the client.

36
01:15.770 --> 01:16.860
Haven't I told you

37
01:16.900 --> 01:18.230
- not to... - "Don't interrupt.

38
01:18.250 --> 01:19.770
Don't yell into the phone.

39
01:20.000 --> 01:22.790
If anything comes up, talk it through calmly.

40
01:22.820 --> 01:24.050
If it's urgent,

41
01:24.070 --> 01:25.740
find something to write it down on.

42
01:25.760 --> 01:27.510
Blah, blah, blah."

43
01:27.530 --> 01:28.530
I remember everything.

44
01:28.550 --> 01:30.690
Then why don't you do any of those things?

45
01:30.710 --> 01:32.750
Come on, Jane. I couldn't get a hold of myself.

46
01:32.860 --> 01:34.250
Everything has been prepped.

47
01:34.270 --> 01:36.280
We've even picked out food menus for the shoot, Jane.

48
01:36.300 --> 01:38.000
How could they just scrap the whole board?

49
01:38.060 --> 01:41.330
Why are you wasting time telling me what I already know?

50
01:41.400 --> 01:43.400
What? Why would you say that?

51
01:44.030 --> 01:45.620
Instead of arguing with the client,

52
01:45.640 --> 01:47.990
shouldn't we change the plans and overload them with info?

53
01:48.160 --> 01:48.870
Huh?

54
01:49.710 --> 01:51.910
What do you mean... "overload them with info"?

55
01:51.930 --> 01:54.320
Where did you learn all these things?

56
01:54.880 --> 01:55.960
Chomphoo told me

57
01:55.980 --> 01:57.450
with a client like Giew,

58
01:57.470 --> 02:00.120
we must overload them with details and confuse them.

59
02:00.410 --> 02:01.790
Then the project will go uninterrupted.

60
02:02.150 --> 02:03.210
Jane.

61
02:03.230 --> 02:04.950
Do you even know what that means?

62
02:05.100 --> 02:06.510
You can only say that when you're with me.

63
02:06.720 --> 02:09.260
You can't say that to our clients, alright?

64
02:09.790 --> 02:10.990
I'm an adult now, Jaab.

65
02:11.110 --> 02:12.200
We're both speaking the same language.

66
02:12.220 --> 02:13.360
You think I don't understand?

67
02:13.630 --> 02:16.190
And will you stop treating me like a baby?

68
02:16.210 --> 02:17.740
Mm...

69
02:17.910 --> 02:19.760
Are you sure...? Huh?

70
02:19.780 --> 02:21.570
The oldest of the bunch?

71
02:21.590 --> 02:23.080
Jaab, stop it...

72
02:23.110 --> 02:24.890
Why? I want to. You got a problem?

73
02:24.910 --> 02:27.080
- Huh? The oldest of the bunch? - Jaab...

74
02:27.100 --> 02:28.200
- Huh? - Hey.

75
02:28.240 --> 02:30.660
You two are all lovey-dovey again.

76
02:30.680 --> 02:31.490
What?

77
02:31.510 --> 02:32.510
How is this any of your business?

78
02:32.680 --> 02:34.690
Go back the way you came.

79
02:41.640 --> 02:43.200
The oldest of the bunch...

80
02:43.370 --> 02:45.430
- I said stop. It hurts. - Ouch.

81
02:45.460 --> 02:47.710
Why did you hit me? That hurt, Jane.

82
02:47.860 --> 02:48.910
This hurts, too.

83
02:49.810 --> 02:51.700
How about this? Does this hurt?

84
02:51.730 --> 02:52.580
I don't think it does...

85
02:52.600 --> 02:54.520
- I said it hurts. - Ouch... Jane.

86
02:54.540 --> 02:55.490
- Take that! - Ouch.

87
03:03.900 --> 03:04.700
What's so funny, Jane?

88
03:07.060 --> 03:07.770
Nothing.

89
03:08.110 --> 03:09.110
Serves you right.

90
03:12.010 --> 03:13.010
What are you laughing at?

91
03:13.720 --> 03:15.690
Nothing. I wasn't laughing.

92
03:16.000 --> 03:17.600
Turn around. Look the other way.

93
03:26.700 --> 03:30.360
It happens on its own without an explanation.

94
03:31.820 --> 03:34.810
There's no exact science behind it. No rules set in stone.

95
03:35.430 --> 03:37.200
It's like an eruption in my heart.

96
03:37.710 --> 03:39.390
There's no way to control

97
03:40.210 --> 03:41.570
the chemistry between two people.

98
05:13.970 --> 05:15.710
We're lucky that Jane managed to convince them

99
05:15.730 --> 05:18.010
that a long shot is only required for the intro.

100
05:18.030 --> 05:20.650
Still, I don't trust you all to improvise out in the field.

101
05:20.730 --> 05:21.700
Come on, Sis.

102
05:21.720 --> 05:22.630
Don't worry.

103
05:22.800 --> 05:24.470
I've talked to Chomphoo about the breaks again.

104
05:24.900 --> 05:26.480
The outsourcing crew will be there later in the day.

105
05:26.510 --> 05:29.120
Our team will handle the blocking in the morning instead.

106
05:29.320 --> 05:30.110
How about that?

107
05:30.130 --> 05:31.940
In the morning?

108
05:32.010 --> 05:32.810
Mm.

109
05:33.080 --> 05:35.050
We’d probably fall behind schedule.

110
05:35.200 --> 05:36.700
Plus, we'd risk missing the light.

111
05:36.910 --> 05:39.730
How about you spend the whole day with the blocking tomorrow?

112
05:39.750 --> 05:42.590
Then we'll pay for another night at the villa.

113
05:42.900 --> 05:44.690
It's better than paying for the OT anyway.

114
05:44.710 --> 05:46.800
Then we'll stay a night there,

115
05:47.020 --> 05:49.440
so that we won't have to travel in the morning. How about that?

116
05:49.710 --> 05:51.620
- Whoa, Sis... - Ooh...

117
05:53.400 --> 05:55.530
You're worried about us?

118
05:55.910 --> 05:57.440
I'm deeply touched.

119
05:57.460 --> 05:59.890
Where can I find a better head of production?

120
06:00.720 --> 06:01.880
Take that!

121
06:02.020 --> 06:04.220
I'm worried about the OT team.

122
06:04.240 --> 06:06.440
Staying a night there is just an added benefit for you all.

123
06:06.460 --> 06:07.300
Oh...

124
06:08.280 --> 06:09.860
That's about it. Okay?

125
06:09.880 --> 06:12.020
By the way, are you coming with us?

126
06:12.240 --> 06:14.640
Jane is already on your team. Why waste more resources?

127
06:15.390 --> 06:18.120
I'm leaving this to you, my right-hand man.

128
06:19.190 --> 06:20.320
You can leave it to me.

129
06:20.900 --> 06:21.880
Jeez...

130
06:21.900 --> 06:24.180
From the time he was an assistant producer

131
06:24.200 --> 06:25.710
now that he’s a producer himself,

132
06:25.730 --> 06:27.120
it's getting quite hard to tell

133
06:27.140 --> 06:28.640
if you're actually assigning tasks

134
06:28.660 --> 06:30.280
or if you're just being lazy.

135
06:32.200 --> 06:33.930
- There's no pen. - Where's a pen?

136
06:34.110 --> 06:35.050
Hey, Khanoon.

137
06:35.090 --> 06:36.200
- Sis... That hurts! - Take that!

138
06:36.230 --> 06:36.970
Take this, too.

139
06:36.990 --> 06:38.430
- Sis, that hurts... Ow! - There!

140
06:38.450 --> 06:39.930
- Another one. - Sis, please!

141
06:40.010 --> 06:40.930
- Please! Ouch! - There!

142
06:41.300 --> 06:42.600
Jane... Jane, save me!

143
06:42.620 --> 06:43.790
- Jane... Jane! - Ugh!

144
06:43.810 --> 06:44.650
I've got another one!

145
06:44.670 --> 06:45.300
- Hey! - Not this one!

146
06:45.320 --> 06:47.020
- Not this one. - This one is expensive.

147
06:47.690 --> 06:48.990
You'll pay for this, Khanoon.

148
06:49.600 --> 06:51.930
Khanoon, didn't I tell you to be quick?

149
06:51.950 --> 06:54.590
If you had come just a bit later, asshole,

150
06:54.610 --> 06:57.210
the fried pork would've all been gone.

151
06:57.580 --> 06:59.720
You didn't invite anyone else. Wouldn't they get upset?

152
07:00.010 --> 07:00.820
It's okay.

153
07:00.840 --> 07:02.420
Jane brought his own food.

154
07:04.010 --> 07:04.730
Hey.

155
07:04.890 --> 07:07.310
I mean the others, not just Jane.

156
07:07.340 --> 07:09.700
Oh...? Am I busted?

157
07:09.720 --> 07:11.150
Aw... What a shame...

158
07:11.390 --> 07:12.520
Don't go overboard.

159
07:12.810 --> 07:13.520
Huh? And...

160
07:13.540 --> 07:14.730
- You got a problem, Khanoon? - Hey, what? Hey!

161
07:14.760 --> 07:16.640
You're always talking about Jane...

162
07:16.670 --> 07:17.750
- Khanoon! Quiet! - Go see Jane, then.

163
07:17.780 --> 07:19.640
- Shit! Come here, asshole! - Why are you kicking me?!

164
07:23.180 --> 07:24.880
- Khanoon, where are you going? - Hey, people...

165
07:24.910 --> 07:26.810
People are working. Be quiet.

166
07:27.210 --> 07:28.080
Hey, stop it...

167
07:28.100 --> 07:28.700
Khanoon...

168
07:28.730 --> 07:30.840
- Don't hide behind Jane. - Look at him. He's a psycho.

169
07:30.860 --> 07:32.020
- Help me. - Jaab.

170
07:39.600 --> 07:40.650
Here you go.

171
07:40.670 --> 07:42.440
You've done well. You can have a piece.

172
07:44.830 --> 07:45.700
By the way...

173
07:46.110 --> 07:47.520
Where are the others, Jane?

174
07:48.110 --> 07:50.650
Bew and Chompoo are having a meal with our client.

175
07:51.380 --> 07:52.650
And the others...

176
07:53.400 --> 07:54.310
I have no clue.

177
08:13.150 --> 08:14.110
So yummy.

178
08:16.700 --> 08:17.330
Why?

179
08:17.350 --> 08:18.590
They couldn't stand him, right?

180
08:19.300 --> 08:20.200
Jaab is too inconsiderate.

181
08:20.410 --> 08:21.360
Come on, Jane.

182
08:21.690 --> 08:22.960
Why are you insulting me?

183
08:30.590 --> 08:31.220
Ow.

184
08:33.210 --> 08:34.210
Sorry.

185
09:07.590 --> 09:08.110
Okay.

186
09:08.130 --> 09:09.370
I'll be going now.

187
09:09.510 --> 09:10.710
- Bye-bye. - See you tomorrow.

188
09:10.730 --> 09:12.490
- See you. - Gotta go before the traffic gets bad.

189
09:12.510 --> 09:13.400
Right. See you.

190
09:13.420 --> 09:14.420
Go home soon.

191
09:19.210 --> 09:20.120
Jane.

192
09:20.140 --> 09:21.380
- Hm? - Are you leaving?

193
09:21.400 --> 09:22.640
It's almost 8 P.M.

194
09:22.790 --> 09:25.900
I'll go after I'm done sending the schedule to the team...

195
09:26.200 --> 09:28.500
Oh, the pickup is at the office tomorrow.

196
09:28.520 --> 09:29.690
6 A.M. sharp.

197
09:29.920 --> 09:31.840
Whoa... Why so early?

198
09:32.120 --> 09:33.990
How do you get to the office?

199
09:34.400 --> 09:35.400
Mm...

200
09:35.910 --> 09:37.170
If you don't mind,

201
09:37.190 --> 09:38.890
can you pick me up at my place?

202
09:40.400 --> 09:41.290
Sure.

203
09:46.490 --> 09:47.910
I'll pick you up.

204
09:55.300 --> 09:56.800
I'm calling you a ride.

205
09:57.210 --> 09:58.440
I've got some discount coupons.

206
09:58.460 --> 09:59.390
Whoa.

207
09:59.410 --> 10:00.300
That's nice.

208
10:03.010 --> 10:04.060
By the way...

209
10:04.320 --> 10:06.900
It's nice that our places are in the same direction, yeah?

210
10:07.510 --> 10:08.290
Mm.

211
10:08.800 --> 10:11.480
We can take turns picking up and dropping each other off.

212
10:11.500 --> 10:12.800
And we can split the fare.

213
10:12.820 --> 10:14.510
It's nice like you said.

214
10:15.910 --> 10:16.910
Yeah.

215
10:17.200 --> 10:18.240
It's nice, yeah?

216
10:20.010 --> 10:20.720
Hm?

217
10:22.310 --> 10:23.510
By the way...

218
10:25.010 --> 10:26.290
Is the ride here yet?

219
10:28.010 --> 10:29.000
There it is.

220
10:29.510 --> 10:30.240
Oh.

221
10:30.850 --> 10:31.900
Okay.

222
10:52.190 --> 10:53.800
What's up, Jane?

223
10:59.610 --> 11:01.120
You drove here yourself, Jaab?

224
11:01.790 --> 11:02.690
Huh?

225
11:02.800 --> 11:04.470
Oh... Yeah.

226
11:16.920 --> 11:17.730
I...

227
11:17.860 --> 11:19.700
I called a ride, but the app found none.

228
11:19.730 --> 11:21.190
I was afraid I'd be running late, so...

229
11:21.800 --> 11:23.350
I drove here myself.

230
11:23.800 --> 11:25.960
I don't usually see you drive, though.

231
11:28.020 --> 11:29.020
And...

232
11:29.610 --> 11:32.100
Which one do you prefer?

233
11:33.120 --> 11:34.120
What?

234
11:34.410 --> 11:35.950
That's up to you.

235
11:36.110 --> 11:37.920
It's your car, and you're the driver.

236
11:38.110 --> 11:39.200
Why are you asking me?

237
11:40.220 --> 11:41.920
I was just asking.

238
11:41.940 --> 11:43.090
So maybe...

239
11:43.270 --> 11:45.010
I'd figure out what I should do.

240
11:46.990 --> 11:48.250
What are you talking about?

241
11:49.210 --> 11:51.170
No... Nothing.

242
11:51.230 --> 11:53.200
Hey, let me help you.

243
11:53.220 --> 11:54.280
Oh, okay.

244
12:48.020 --> 12:48.810
Want some?

245
12:55.430 --> 12:56.370
I'm good, Jane.

246
12:56.510 --> 12:59.240
My hands are full. I'm driving, you see.

247
13:01.600 --> 13:02.370
Here.

248
13:13.300 --> 13:15.110
You brought snacks like a kid, Jane.

249
13:18.420 --> 13:19.870
I'll be away for a few days,

250
13:20.320 --> 13:21.690
and I'm worried about their glow-up.

251
13:23.630 --> 13:24.380
Hm?

252
13:25.700 --> 13:27.100
Who and whose glow-up?

253
13:33.000 --> 13:34.490
What glow-up is he talking about?

254
13:51.200 --> 13:52.500
Whose glow-up?

255
13:53.500 --> 13:55.100
Who is he talking about?

256
13:57.900 --> 13:58.900
Jane.

257
13:59.610 --> 14:01.730
Who... Whose glow-up again?

258
14:03.680 --> 14:04.130
This one.

259
14:05.050 --> 14:06.120
I'll be away for three days.

260
14:06.210 --> 14:08.520
They will glow up and turn brown, and I won't get to enjoy them.

261
14:08.900 --> 14:10.240
Oh...

262
14:10.260 --> 14:11.220
You're afraid the grapes would turn...

263
14:11.240 --> 14:11.770
Jane!

264
14:11.910 --> 14:12.700
Come on.

265
14:13.610 --> 14:15.000
Wait... I'll get our stuff.

266
14:16.960 --> 14:17.800
Jane!

267
14:44.900 --> 14:46.620
Gosh...

268
14:46.640 --> 14:48.670
We're finally here!

269
14:49.100 --> 14:50.110
Damn,

270
14:50.290 --> 14:52.060
it took forever to get here.

271
14:54.120 --> 14:56.200
My back is killing me.

272
15:03.730 --> 15:04.580
Oh...

273
15:04.600 --> 15:06.600
I'm so sorry, Jane.

274
15:06.710 --> 15:07.830
It's just that...

275
15:07.850 --> 15:09.560
you're below my eye level.

276
15:09.580 --> 15:10.420
Jaab...

277
15:16.910 --> 15:18.290
- Khanoon. - Huh?

278
15:18.320 --> 15:19.390
I'm waiting

279
15:19.410 --> 15:22.320
for the day Jane calls Jaab an asshole.

280
15:22.340 --> 15:23.660
The beers are on me.

281
15:23.680 --> 15:24.200
Oh?

282
15:24.220 --> 15:25.400
- Was that a promise? - Yes!

283
15:25.420 --> 15:27.000
- Don't take it back, okay? - Yeah.

284
15:27.020 --> 15:27.760
Oh...

285
15:28.110 --> 15:30.520
I think... For someone like Jaab,

286
15:30.540 --> 15:31.610
it won't be long

287
15:32.500 --> 15:33.690
until we get free beers.

288
15:33.710 --> 15:35.180
- Don't take it back, okay? - Yeah!

289
15:35.200 --> 15:35.990
Alright.

290
15:40.040 --> 15:41.910
Jaab, can you just drink it properly?

291
15:44.810 --> 15:46.300
Goodness...

292
15:47.200 --> 15:47.960
Brother,

293
15:48.320 --> 15:50.520
you were doing just fine drinking packs of beer,

294
15:50.540 --> 15:53.130
but now... you are choking on a can of soda?

295
15:53.590 --> 15:54.910
Whoa, Khanoon.

296
15:54.930 --> 15:56.530
You fucking...

297
15:58.390 --> 16:01.010
You're better off choking on that soda. Don't argue just yet.

298
16:01.080 --> 16:02.210
Come on, Jane!

299
16:02.770 --> 16:04.010
Drink it properly, come on.

300
16:04.090 --> 16:06.410
That sounded so gentle, but it hit like a truck.

301
16:06.920 --> 16:07.850
Hey, Sis.

302
16:08.100 --> 16:09.240
You're with them, too?

303
16:11.620 --> 16:12.390
Come on, Khanoon.

304
16:12.410 --> 16:13.520
- Right. - Let's do it again.

305
16:13.540 --> 16:15.610
Gosh... Taking up the SD card for nothing.

306
16:15.630 --> 16:17.000
Alright. Ready.

307
16:17.020 --> 16:17.980
Action.

308
16:19.200 --> 16:22.120
Just pretend to drink it. Choking again would waste our time.

309
16:26.240 --> 16:27.050
Here's how it goes.

310
16:27.120 --> 16:28.660
After I chug down the soda,

311
16:28.690 --> 16:30.000
pan the camera to the pool.

312
16:30.020 --> 16:31.780
I'll have two extras jump into it.

313
16:31.890 --> 16:32.890
Mm.

314
16:33.720 --> 16:35.390
Jane will demonstrate the scene.

315
16:35.410 --> 16:36.820
Jane, jump into the pool.

316
16:56.900 --> 16:59.120
And what's next?

317
16:59.500 --> 17:00.410
Huh?

318
17:01.390 --> 17:02.160
Right.

319
17:02.500 --> 17:03.500
Uh...

320
17:04.300 --> 17:05.610
I think it still doesn't flow smoothly.

321
17:06.400 --> 17:07.100
How about this?

322
17:07.210 --> 17:08.450
Two extras will bump into each other,

323
17:08.480 --> 17:09.920
and both will fall into the pool.

324
17:10.120 --> 17:11.800
- Mm. - Okay.

325
17:12.110 --> 17:13.110
I'll show you.

326
17:16.410 --> 17:17.170
Jane.

327
17:17.310 --> 17:18.130
Get up.

328
17:20.330 --> 17:22.520
Listen. This is how it goes.

329
17:22.540 --> 17:23.960
After you shoot the lead,

330
17:23.980 --> 17:25.380
shift the focus to the background.

331
17:25.550 --> 17:27.280
After I give you the cue by bumping into an extra

332
17:27.300 --> 17:28.790
and knocking him into the pool,

333
17:28.810 --> 17:29.900
you do a still frame there.

334
17:29.920 --> 17:32.520
I'll use CGI to add a water splash later.

335
17:32.540 --> 17:33.420
It goes like this.

336
17:36.820 --> 17:37.340
Whoa!

337
17:52.560 --> 17:53.560
That's it.

338
17:55.890 --> 17:57.000
End of the scene.

339
17:58.900 --> 18:00.400
Are you trying to kill me or what?

340
18:00.800 --> 18:03.100
Come on, Jane. It has to look realistic.

341
18:03.130 --> 18:03.840
Let me take a look...

342
18:04.020 --> 18:05.530
Oh, realistic?

343
18:05.690 --> 18:06.950
If that's what you're going for,

344
18:07.100 --> 18:08.840
how about we both jump into the pool?

345
18:09.200 --> 18:10.200
Oh?

346
18:10.700 --> 18:11.750
Together, alright?

347
18:12.910 --> 18:13.810
Jaab.

348
18:15.240 --> 18:16.240
By the way, Jane,

349
18:16.260 --> 18:18.400
there's a scene of an extra chilling on the rooftop.

350
18:18.420 --> 18:19.810
Please climb up there, okay?

351
18:19.830 --> 18:22.990
It's full of lizards up there, Jane.

352
18:24.600 --> 18:25.910
Please?

353
18:26.830 --> 18:29.740
Once we're done here... can we work on another scene

354
18:29.760 --> 18:30.820
so that we don't waste our time?

355
18:32.510 --> 18:34.210
Okay, that works.

356
18:41.500 --> 18:42.400
Come on, Jane.

357
18:42.420 --> 18:43.500
Throw it, Jane.

358
18:43.520 --> 18:45.960
Make sure you throw it right on my head here.

359
18:45.990 --> 18:46.990
- Jaab. - Right here.

360
18:47.280 --> 18:49.790
You're on the duck. How am I supposed to throw it right through?

361
18:49.910 --> 18:50.610
Huh?

362
18:50.710 --> 18:52.450
Jane... What was that?

363
18:52.500 --> 18:53.950
Jane? Huh?

364
18:54.110 --> 18:55.870
I couldn't hear you, Jane.

365
18:55.900 --> 18:56.710
Jane?

366
18:56.900 --> 18:57.720
Ow!

367
18:58.110 --> 18:59.990
- Cut. We're done. - Nice.

368
19:00.010 --> 19:01.010
How was it?

369
19:01.210 --> 19:02.370
Good. That was easy.

370
19:14.600 --> 19:17.110
Here's a rough cut. Take a look.

371
19:17.210 --> 19:18.090
Let me take a look.

372
19:19.900 --> 19:21.290
Mm...

373
19:21.320 --> 19:22.320
Khanoon.

374
19:23.320 --> 19:24.610
I think the framing is a bit too tight.

375
19:24.630 --> 19:26.640
Maybe step back a bit for the actual shoot.

376
19:26.660 --> 19:28.610
And at the end, keep the still frame a bit longer.

377
19:28.630 --> 19:30.090
We might be able to use it later.

378
19:30.900 --> 19:31.990
Okay...

379
19:32.110 --> 19:33.230
I'll make some changes...

380
19:33.610 --> 19:34.610
Oh, Jaab.

381
19:35.220 --> 19:37.600
Does this spot work for this scene?

382
19:38.440 --> 19:39.920
Um...

383
19:40.040 --> 19:41.500
It's fine by me, yeah.

384
19:41.520 --> 19:42.720
Mm, okay.

385
19:42.790 --> 19:43.830
Here, here.

386
19:43.850 --> 19:45.730
I fixed it like you said. Take a look.

387
19:45.910 --> 19:47.690
- What? Are you The Flash or what? - Of course.

388
19:47.920 --> 19:50.000
- What? - I've been doing this my whole life.

389
19:50.210 --> 19:51.140
If it looks rushed...

390
19:51.160 --> 19:52.480
Look at these scenes.

391
19:52.810 --> 19:54.210
- Right, like I told you. - I reframed...

392
19:54.230 --> 19:55.100
Yeah.

393
19:55.300 --> 19:56.600
- And... - Sheesh!

394
19:56.800 --> 19:58.890
Not too shabby.

395
20:00.300 --> 20:01.300
It kinda works...

396
20:01.790 --> 20:03.110
Yeah, yeah.

397
20:05.820 --> 20:07.000
And then this...

398
20:07.030 --> 20:08.700
Yeah, that one...

399
20:08.720 --> 20:10.400
- Okay... - Yeah.

400
20:10.500 --> 20:11.650
Color grade...

401
20:26.610 --> 20:27.420
Hey.

402
20:28.500 --> 20:29.420
- What? - Come here.

403
20:30.810 --> 20:32.100
Your teeth

404
20:32.200 --> 20:33.890
are sticking out like a sore thumb.

405
20:37.900 --> 20:40.980
Then... I'll sink them into your skull.

406
20:41.010 --> 20:41.930
Shut up!

407
20:42.410 --> 20:43.410
You're ruining the mood.

408
20:52.430 --> 20:53.360
What are you looking at, Jaab?

409
20:54.490 --> 20:55.680
It's... It's nothing, Jane.

410
20:55.820 --> 20:56.410
Nothing, really.

411
20:56.430 --> 20:58.880
Khanoon is killing it with the editing...

412
20:58.910 --> 20:59.910
I'm delighted.

413
21:00.100 --> 21:01.900
Nothing... Nothing, Jaab...

414
21:05.800 --> 21:07.270
I'm gonna save it now, okay?

415
21:07.290 --> 21:08.200
Right.

416
21:08.220 --> 21:09.220
Okay.

417
21:16.120 --> 21:18.710
Sheesh, Jane.

418
21:20.900 --> 21:22.900
You bought the same jacket as me?

419
21:26.220 --> 21:27.290
I bought mine ages ago.

420
21:29.690 --> 21:30.760
An auspicious color?

421
21:32.300 --> 21:33.590
I don't believe in that stuff.

422
21:33.610 --> 21:34.680
Mm...

423
21:35.210 --> 21:36.280
Neither do I.

424
21:36.900 --> 21:38.400
But my older brother

425
21:38.420 --> 21:39.510
is very into it.

426
21:40.010 --> 21:40.930
You mean Jeng?

427
21:41.090 --> 21:42.010
Mm.

428
21:43.390 --> 21:46.020
His looks say the opposite, yeah?

429
21:47.110 --> 21:49.640
If you said it was you who believed in that stuff,

430
21:50.110 --> 21:51.800
I think that would be more believable.

431
21:53.000 --> 21:56.320
When did you see... how Jeng dresses up?

432
21:56.340 --> 22:00.040
Well... He drove me to work a week ago.

433
22:00.790 --> 22:01.440
Oh...

434
22:01.460 --> 22:03.640
He looks more composed than you do.

435
22:04.210 --> 22:05.290
Mm...

436
22:05.310 --> 22:09.380
- He looks more composed than I do, huh? - Ouch!

437
22:09.690 --> 22:10.820
- Ow! - Take that.

438
22:10.840 --> 22:12.150
You're fighting back now, Jane?

439
22:12.490 --> 22:13.480
- Mm. - Whoa, Jane.

440
22:13.620 --> 22:14.730
- There... - Jane.

441
22:16.850 --> 22:17.690
Come on.

442
22:17.710 --> 22:19.080
Jane... Jane.

443
22:19.560 --> 22:20.780
You're hitting me way too hard.

444
22:20.800 --> 22:21.510
Ow...

445
22:21.530 --> 22:22.390
It's over.

446
22:22.610 --> 22:23.300
Ow.

447
22:23.600 --> 22:24.420
Ow...

448
22:24.840 --> 22:25.500
Jaab...

449
22:26.410 --> 22:26.960
Hey.

450
22:26.980 --> 22:27.980
You're done.

451
22:28.040 --> 22:30.090
Let's see how long you will last, Jane.

452
22:47.400 --> 22:48.840
What is it that you have against me?

453
22:50.290 --> 22:51.520
Am I allowed to have you?

454
22:52.600 --> 22:53.530
Have what now?

455
22:56.160 --> 22:56.830
Oh...

456
22:58.330 --> 23:00.190
Nothing, Jane. Nothing.

457
23:00.720 --> 23:01.490
Gosh.

458
23:02.340 --> 23:04.040
You're robbing me of my sleep.

459
23:04.800 --> 23:06.680
I should've shared a room with Khanoon instead.

460
23:09.180 --> 23:10.460
How could you say that?

461
23:10.480 --> 23:11.520
You can't sleep,

462
23:11.540 --> 23:13.200
I can't either.

463
23:13.810 --> 23:14.710
Enough.

464
23:14.920 --> 23:15.880
I'm gonna sleep now.

465
23:17.030 --> 23:19.110
Hey, Jane. Wait.

466
23:19.610 --> 23:20.570
You're sleeping now?

467
23:42.500 --> 23:43.500
Jane?

468
23:44.010 --> 23:45.010
Are you asleep?

469
23:46.130 --> 23:47.080
Jane?

470
23:47.710 --> 23:48.710
Are you sleeping?

471
23:53.660 --> 23:55.160
Jane, are you asleep?

472
23:55.380 --> 23:56.440
Jane...

473
23:57.040 --> 23:58.230
Jaab...

474
24:04.880 --> 24:06.610
Jane, are you... Oops.

475
24:08.420 --> 24:09.570
I'm sorry.

476
24:11.000 --> 24:11.840
I'm going to sleep now.

477
24:39.210 --> 24:39.910
Camera.

478
24:40.800 --> 24:41.520
Speed.

479
24:41.640 --> 24:44.730
Three, two, and... Action.

480
24:58.010 --> 24:59.700
Okay, cut.

481
25:00.510 --> 25:02.910
Okay. Onto the next scene.

482
25:03.080 --> 25:03.940
Okay.

483
25:03.960 --> 25:06.510
Onto the next scene. Reset, everyone.

484
25:10.280 --> 25:12.100
Hey, Ice. What's the next scene?

485
25:12.420 --> 25:13.540
Oh, it's...

486
25:13.560 --> 25:15.030
The next scene is in the living room.

487
25:15.300 --> 25:16.300
Oh, okay, okay.

488
25:25.900 --> 25:28.100
Whose meal box is this, Nat?

489
25:28.300 --> 25:29.510
It's Jaab's, Jane.

490
25:29.530 --> 25:31.030
It has been left open for a while.

491
25:31.050 --> 25:33.530
It's probably stale now, so I'm getting him a fresh one.

492
25:34.300 --> 25:35.470
Bring him a new one, okay?

493
25:35.790 --> 25:37.190
Force him to eat it, too.

494
25:37.210 --> 25:38.210
And tell him that

495
25:38.610 --> 25:40.790
this is Jannarong's order.

496
25:41.000 --> 25:42.240
Understood.

497
25:42.630 --> 25:43.480
Understood.

498
25:43.690 --> 25:45.080
I'll eat it right now.

499
26:06.120 --> 26:06.880
Jaab.

500
26:07.880 --> 26:09.050
Your stomach is empty,

501
26:09.080 --> 26:10.200
why are you drinking a soda?

502
26:11.400 --> 26:12.710
Who says it's empty, Jane?

503
26:12.730 --> 26:15.720
I took a big bite just now.

504
26:16.810 --> 26:18.640
What will you do if you have a stomachache?

505
26:19.900 --> 26:20.900
Hey...

506
26:21.200 --> 26:23.480
Is Mr. Jannarong worried about me?

507
26:23.700 --> 26:25.170
Yes, I am.

508
26:27.320 --> 26:28.600
I don't want to take you to a hospital.

509
26:30.410 --> 26:31.950
Also, it would be bad if the shoot had to stop.

510
26:32.470 --> 26:35.170
Your role is irreplaceable, you know?

511
26:39.110 --> 26:40.110
Finish it already.

512
26:41.990 --> 26:43.310
The set is ready to go.

513
26:44.680 --> 26:45.290
Whoa.

514
26:46.310 --> 26:48.010
Here's the paper towel.

515
26:49.680 --> 26:50.680
Hey, Jaab!

516
26:51.520 --> 26:52.980
Thank you, Mr. Jannarong.

517
26:53.000 --> 26:54.000
See you.

518
27:05.000 --> 27:07.490
Jaab, have you been feeling a bit down today?

519
27:07.600 --> 27:09.560
Why did we have to reshoot the long take several times?

520
27:09.900 --> 27:11.600
Because you sucked at your job.

521
27:11.810 --> 27:12.740
What do you want me to do?

522
27:12.760 --> 27:14.920
Want me to hand it in like this?

523
27:15.000 --> 27:16.480
No way.

524
27:16.610 --> 27:17.770
Stop rambling.

525
27:17.790 --> 27:19.200
We'll reshoot it if it turns out bad.

526
27:19.810 --> 27:21.200
I sucked at my job?

527
27:21.220 --> 27:22.220
Yeah.

528
27:22.490 --> 27:23.720
Damn it...

529
27:23.740 --> 27:25.370
It's always my fault.

530
27:27.900 --> 27:28.620
Here.

531
27:30.340 --> 27:31.340
A vitamin drink.

532
27:32.750 --> 27:33.830
Drink it, Jaab.

533
27:34.010 --> 27:35.630
You'll sleep deeply in the van,

534
27:35.650 --> 27:37.120
and you won't wake up with a headache.

535
27:37.310 --> 27:38.890
Thank you for worrying about me.

536
27:40.570 --> 27:42.510
This is for you, Khanoon.

537
27:42.530 --> 27:44.090
Oh, thank you.

538
27:44.190 --> 27:46.270
And this one is for you, Chomphoo.

539
27:46.300 --> 27:49.240
Thank you, Jane, my darling.

540
27:49.810 --> 27:51.910
Also, the van is waiting in front of the house.

541
27:51.930 --> 27:53.330
- We can just leave after packing up our stuff. - What?!

542
27:53.360 --> 27:53.860
Okay.

543
27:53.880 --> 27:55.550
- Gosh, and you're telling me that just now? - Let's go.

544
27:55.570 --> 27:56.830
- Come on, come on. - Let's go.

545
27:56.850 --> 27:57.910
I'm leaving.

546
27:58.610 --> 27:59.680
I'll sleep in the front seat.

547
28:00.010 --> 28:01.300
You're staying here or what?

548
28:01.720 --> 28:02.490
I'm leaving.

549
28:03.200 --> 28:04.040
Come on, Jaab.

550
28:04.180 --> 28:05.510
Get up already, Jaab.

551
28:05.770 --> 28:06.600
Come on.

552
28:11.110 --> 28:12.410
"Get up already, Jaab..."

553
28:13.210 --> 28:14.100
Got it,

554
28:14.120 --> 28:15.530
"my darling."

555
28:27.590 --> 28:29.010
Oh...

556
28:29.610 --> 28:31.110
We've finally arrived!

557
28:32.500 --> 28:33.500
Don't forget your bag.

558
28:33.690 --> 28:34.690
Hey, wait...

559
28:34.730 --> 28:35.900
Let me move the seat for you.

560
28:46.610 --> 28:47.780
Jeez.

561
28:51.400 --> 28:53.580
I think I'm going to work on the documents for a bit first.

562
28:53.600 --> 28:54.850
Just head home without me.

563
28:55.820 --> 28:56.940
I'm good.

564
28:56.970 --> 28:57.750
I can wait.

565
28:58.120 --> 28:59.120
Are you sure?

566
28:59.140 --> 29:00.200
Mm.

567
29:00.680 --> 29:01.300
Gosh.

568
29:01.320 --> 29:03.120
So you two are staying?

569
29:03.140 --> 29:03.900
Mm.

570
29:03.920 --> 29:04.920
I'm leaving, then.

571
29:05.210 --> 29:06.800
- It's getting late. - Hey, Khanoon.

572
29:07.000 --> 29:09.240
Are you going to BTS? You can come with me. I'll pass by.

573
29:09.920 --> 29:10.910
Jackpot.

574
29:10.940 --> 29:12.610
- I can't say no to that. - Okay.

575
29:13.320 --> 29:14.520
- Let's go. - We'll be going now.

576
29:14.540 --> 29:15.460
- Bye-bye. - See you. Bye.

577
29:15.480 --> 29:16.720
See you. Good luck.

578
29:16.740 --> 29:17.530
See ya.

579
29:19.290 --> 29:20.090
Let's go.

580
29:20.110 --> 29:21.000
Mm.

581
29:38.090 --> 29:39.710
It's almost done.

582
29:39.890 --> 29:41.080
Can we stay for another 30 minutes?

583
29:41.510 --> 29:42.510
Mm.

584
29:56.940 --> 29:57.710
Jane.

585
29:58.000 --> 29:58.700
Hm?

586
30:16.910 --> 30:17.910
What is it?

587
30:19.400 --> 30:20.100
Uh...

588
30:21.200 --> 30:21.920
What was it again?

589
30:22.300 --> 30:23.790
I forgot what I was going to say.

590
30:27.210 --> 30:29.090
There are some oranges in the fridge.

591
30:29.210 --> 30:30.210
Those are mine.

592
30:31.010 --> 30:32.490
How about you eat them while you wait?

593
30:36.010 --> 30:37.010
Jane...

594
30:37.300 --> 30:38.950
You're a pest.

595
30:40.320 --> 30:41.440
- What? - Huh?

596
30:41.690 --> 30:43.280
You had grapes yesterday,

597
30:43.410 --> 30:44.730
and you've got oranges today.

598
30:45.020 --> 30:47.680
Jane... You're like a pest.

599
30:48.830 --> 30:50.720
I'm not a pest.

600
31:13.900 --> 31:14.840
Is that song too old for you?

601
31:15.300 --> 31:17.000
We're the same age, Jaab.

602
31:17.600 --> 31:18.600
Why would it be too old for me?

603
31:18.900 --> 31:20.000
Sheesh.

604
31:20.020 --> 31:21.400
So you know what it is.

605
31:21.430 --> 31:22.130
No.

606
31:23.200 --> 31:24.010
What?

607
31:24.210 --> 31:25.340
Mr. Jannarong.

608
31:28.900 --> 31:30.400
If that's the case,

609
31:30.500 --> 31:32.650
look it up.

610
31:35.560 --> 31:36.890
[Shinme chōdai]

611
31:46.810 --> 31:48.160
Are you saying I'm a caterpillar, Jaab?

612
31:48.920 --> 31:50.300
I'll be going now.

613
32:14.910 --> 32:15.910
It looks lovely on you.

614
32:16.500 --> 32:17.810
Stop it, Jaab.

615
32:18.070 --> 32:19.080
I didn't do anything.

616
32:19.310 --> 32:21.130
I'm giving you a hair treatment.

617
32:23.510 --> 32:25.120
I'm not messing with you, really.

618
32:25.400 --> 32:26.440
Orange peels

619
32:26.590 --> 32:28.240
are good for your hair, Jane.

620
32:28.260 --> 32:29.880
That's what my mom used to tell me.

621
32:31.310 --> 32:32.110
I know.

622
32:32.140 --> 32:32.860
Huh?

623
32:33.180 --> 32:35.080
Then... Why are you so upset?

624
32:35.500 --> 32:37.200
The peels need to be extracted first.

625
32:37.320 --> 32:39.200
Putting them on my head like this

626
32:39.380 --> 32:40.820
will lure the ants in.

627
32:41.090 --> 32:42.090
Oh, I see...

628
32:43.000 --> 32:44.110
Sorry about that, Jane.

629
32:44.130 --> 32:47.880
I might have missed some details...

630
32:49.410 --> 32:50.890
Okay, it looks the same as before now.

631
33:10.510 --> 33:12.700
Here. Time to recharge.

632
33:15.610 --> 33:17.390
I'm good. You can eat it.

633
33:23.320 --> 33:25.480
Choo-choo, chugga, chugga.

634
33:25.500 --> 33:27.570
Choo-choo, chugga, chugga.

635
33:27.590 --> 33:29.500
Choo-choo...

636
33:36.270 --> 33:37.270
Here.

637
33:49.190 --> 33:50.840
So freaking cute.

638
33:52.930 --> 33:53.740
- Uh... - Hm?

639
33:53.760 --> 33:54.600
Well...

640
33:54.620 --> 33:55.980
I, I mean...

641
33:56.070 --> 33:57.960
I mean...

642
33:57.980 --> 33:59.600
I...

643
34:00.790 --> 34:02.530
Don't you think that I'm so freaking cute, Jane?

644
34:05.100 --> 34:06.080
Like a flower, Jane.

645
34:06.390 --> 34:08.030
Am I adorable?

646
34:11.210 --> 34:12.350
No?

647
34:14.300 --> 34:15.910
It's all done. Let's go home.

648
34:17.400 --> 34:18.400
Really?

649
34:19.200 --> 34:20.200
Okay.

650
34:30.700 --> 34:32.200
What the hell am I doing?

651
35:08.900 --> 35:10.600
Text me when you're back at your place.

652
35:11.220 --> 35:12.610
Understood,

653
35:12.710 --> 35:14.420
Mr. Jannarong.

654
35:14.930 --> 35:17.310
Thanks for picking me up and dropping me off,

655
35:17.330 --> 35:18.490
Mr. Phongkitti.

656
35:19.010 --> 35:19.770
I'll get going now.

657
35:19.790 --> 35:20.980
Bye-bye.

658
35:21.000 --> 35:22.000
Bye.

659
35:26.060 --> 35:27.870
"Mr. Phongkitti..."

660
35:55.190 --> 35:55.810
[You aren't at your place yet? I'm going to sleep soon]

661
35:59.810 --> 36:01.490
You're not back at your place yet?

662
36:01.510 --> 36:02.640
I'm going to sleep soon.

663
36:02.900 --> 36:04.380
Sheesh...

664
36:06.590 --> 36:08.000
You read my messages so quickly.

665
36:09.300 --> 36:10.300
Uh...

666
36:14.410 --> 36:17.940
[Jaab: Just took a shower. I didn't tell you because I thought you went to sleep. Sorry]

667
36:17.960 --> 36:19.000
Okay.

668
36:20.900 --> 36:22.100
His reply is so short...

669
36:22.430 --> 36:23.500
Is he mad at me?

670
36:26.750 --> 36:27.750
Uh...

671
36:34.420 --> 36:35.820
Going to bed already? @แก้ ลบ[]

672
36:37.710 --> 36:38.700
Yeah.

673
36:44.930 --> 36:46.620
How are you replying to me, then? @แก้ ลบ[]

674
36:52.310 --> 36:54.120
So cute... Damn it...

675
37:08.300 --> 37:09.310
Gosh.

676
37:09.400 --> 37:11.010
The soundtrack is so sad.

677
37:11.210 --> 37:11.830
True.

678
37:12.110 --> 37:14.240
I'm in a happy relationship,

679
37:14.400 --> 37:15.680
but listening to this...

680
37:15.700 --> 37:17.550
feels like I'm going through a heartbreak.

681
37:18.900 --> 37:20.400
According to the briefing,

682
37:20.540 --> 37:22.960
it appears that our client already has their lead characters.

683
37:23.510 --> 37:25.600
It seems that they're taking care of the actors themselves.

684
37:25.990 --> 37:27.370
Mm. Fantastic.

685
37:27.420 --> 37:29.800
All that's left for us is proposing ideas, right?

686
37:30.300 --> 37:33.660
Do we need to pitch? Or did the client already choose us?

687
37:33.680 --> 37:35.490
They chose us, Bew.

688
37:35.690 --> 37:37.880
It seems that this client is friends with Mon.

689
37:37.900 --> 37:40.390
They once hired us to promote their company.

690
37:40.690 --> 37:42.540
Word probably got around.

691
37:42.570 --> 37:43.390
Fantastic.

692
37:44.690 --> 37:45.800
If that's so...

693
37:46.010 --> 37:48.010
For this MV,

694
37:48.030 --> 37:50.110
you'll be the director once again, Jaab.

695
37:50.130 --> 37:50.650
Gosh.

696
37:50.870 --> 37:53.340
You say it as if we had other directors.

697
37:53.740 --> 37:54.690
You!

698
37:54.710 --> 37:56.220
I'm kidding.

699
37:56.240 --> 37:58.080
I can't tease you at all.

700
37:58.990 --> 38:00.740
When is the deadline, Pun?

701
38:01.000 --> 38:02.160
This one isn't urgent.

702
38:02.490 --> 38:04.430
They want us to finalize the storyboard by next week.

703
38:04.720 --> 38:05.600
Damn it, Pun.

704
38:06.510 --> 38:08.040
Not urgent, my ass.

705
38:09.090 --> 38:09.600
Jeez...

706
38:09.720 --> 38:10.480
Jaab,

707
38:10.850 --> 38:13.080
it's time to disappear into your mind palace.

708
38:13.700 --> 38:14.420
Right.

709
38:14.450 --> 38:17.540
Tomorrow, come to the office and get everything done.

710
38:17.570 --> 38:19.080
And for next week,

711
38:19.110 --> 38:20.990
you'll be working from home for the entire week.

712
38:21.190 --> 38:22.550
After that,

713
38:22.580 --> 38:25.770
you can go wherever you want. But...

714
38:26.000 --> 38:30.000
come back and give us some brilliant ideas as usual, sweetie.

715
38:30.120 --> 38:31.520
Mm...

716
38:31.540 --> 38:32.700
Sure, sweetie.

717
38:33.010 --> 38:34.620
But with this project,

718
38:34.640 --> 38:37.020
will I get some pocket money, beautiful?

719
38:38.130 --> 38:40.470
Of course, handsome.

720
38:40.650 --> 38:44.090
But it will come from your bonus.

721
38:44.170 --> 38:45.060
Okay?

722
38:45.220 --> 38:46.130
Gosh.

723
38:49.610 --> 38:51.050
What are you laughing at, you pest?

724
38:52.510 --> 38:52.990
Oh?

725
38:53.210 --> 38:54.210
This means that...

726
38:54.230 --> 38:55.610
our team is free, then?

727
38:55.780 --> 38:56.450
Sis,

728
38:56.620 --> 38:58.490
can I go on a vacation?

729
38:58.690 --> 38:59.390
Jeez.

730
38:59.410 --> 39:00.690
Why bother?

731
39:00.720 --> 39:02.160
You'll be working from home either way.

732
39:02.510 --> 39:04.380
I'll talk to the higher-ups.

733
39:04.410 --> 39:06.100
You'll be back

734
39:06.120 --> 39:08.230
around the same time Jaab returns with his brilliant ideas.

735
39:09.020 --> 39:11.550
And Jane, you said that you'd be taking a short leave.

736
39:11.700 --> 39:13.520
No need to hand me the document.

737
39:13.540 --> 39:14.800
Consider this your short leave.

738
39:15.400 --> 39:17.830
- Thank you. - My...

739
39:22.290 --> 39:23.200
What?

740
39:23.260 --> 39:24.830
What a wonderful boss.

741
39:25.010 --> 39:26.890
There's no one else like you.

742
39:26.920 --> 39:29.060
Not even in the next life.

743
39:31.210 --> 39:32.790
What a great boss...

744
39:32.810 --> 39:33.920
Such a wonderful boss.

745
39:33.940 --> 39:34.580
Hey.

746
39:34.800 --> 39:35.950
- Wait. - Hm?

747
39:36.100 --> 39:37.720
Why am I the only one

748
39:38.000 --> 39:39.690
working here?

749
39:44.910 --> 39:46.440
It's okay.

750
39:46.460 --> 39:48.520
We've been friends for ten years.

751
39:48.540 --> 39:49.800
Just you wait.

752
39:49.820 --> 39:53.290
I'll make sure you feel like you're on a vacation.

753
39:53.310 --> 39:54.740
When I get to leave for a trip with my partner,

754
39:54.760 --> 39:57.250
I'll call you night and day.

755
39:57.270 --> 39:59.010
At every breakfast, lunch, and dinner,

756
39:59.030 --> 40:00.180
I'll send you photos.

757
40:00.200 --> 40:03.300
So you won't feel like you're being left out.

758
40:03.560 --> 40:04.560
How does that sound, buddy?

759
40:05.400 --> 40:06.400
Thanks a lot.

760
40:06.420 --> 40:07.530
Of course. Don't mention it.

761
40:07.550 --> 40:08.730
You're so, so, cringe.

762
40:08.750 --> 40:09.520
Gosh...

763
40:10.290 --> 40:11.010
Want some?

764
40:18.710 --> 40:19.290
Mm.

765
40:20.340 --> 40:21.090
Mm!

766
40:21.370 --> 40:22.240
That's good!

767
40:22.810 --> 40:24.840
- Hey, Jane. - Chew it first. I'm not in a hurry.

768
40:27.000 --> 40:28.000
Jane,

769
40:28.030 --> 40:29.310
you said the same thing, huh?

770
40:31.020 --> 40:32.360
What... What do you mean?

771
40:38.620 --> 40:39.780
What are you working on?

772
40:39.810 --> 40:40.890
